# Tab ID Lookup and Session/Browser Context Checks

## Tab ID Lookup

The code retrieves a WebContents object from a tab ID:

```cpp
auto* contents = electron::api::WebContents::FromID(target.tab_id);
if (!contents) {
  *error_out = absl::StrFormat("No tab with id: %d", target.tab_id);
  return false;
}
```

This lookup returns null if the specified tab doesn't exist, triggering an error response.

## Browser Context Validation

Multiple functions validate the browser context before proceeding:

```cpp
if (!browser_context()) {
  Release();  // Matches the `AddRef()` in `Run()`.
  return;
}
```

The code prevents further operations when the browser context becomes invalid during async operations.

## Extension Registry Checks

Before executing scripts, the system verifies the extension remains enabled:

```cpp
ExtensionRegistry* registry = ExtensionRegistry::Get(browser_context());
if (!extension() ||
    !registry->enabled_extensions().Contains(extension_id())) {
  Release();
  return;
}
```

This ensures uninstalled or unloaded extensions cannot complete pending operations.

